namics more. So we keep vote for C.\n\nWe need to reference explicit facts: C makes correct decisions quickly, creates positive atmosphere, understands complicated technology; B can be grumpy, makes nasty remarks, weak numeric memory. Also mention that stress resilience for C not explicitly given but we can note that quick correct decisions imply ability under pressure? But we must not infer beyond facts. We have no explicit stress resilience for C, but we can note that quick correct decisions are valuable under pressure. That's acceptable as inference? Might be okay as linking fact to criterion.\n\nWe must produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\". Let's craft."}
